                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                is p.r.a. then it
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserves
                connected limits, and in particular preserves
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monad"} cartesian monad
            %li
              %p
                Conversely, a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                between
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+categories"} presheaf categories
                is p.r.a. if it preserves
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+limits"} connected limits
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                preserves connected limits, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
                preserves all small limits, and a limit-preserving functor from a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cototal+category"} cototal category
                such as a presheaf category to a locally small category is a right adjoint.
            %li
              %p
                Any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+functor"} polynomial functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi h
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mi g
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_h \Pi_g f^*
                is p.r.a., since then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
                can be identified with
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mi g
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_g f^*
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Σ
                          %mi f
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mi g
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_f \; g^*
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+category"} presheaf category
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\colon E \to Set
                is p.r.a., then the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set/T
                (also called the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Artin+gluing"} Artin gluing
                in this context) is again a presheaf category. Conversely, if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set/T
                is a presheaf category, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                preserves connected limits, and thus is p.r.a.
            %li
              %p
                A parametric right adjoint functor (with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small
                codomain) has in particular a left
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multi-adjoint"} multi-adjoint
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\in B
                to the family of all units
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mrow
                            %mi b
                            %mo ,
                            %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mi b
                        %mo →
                        %mi T
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_{b,i} : b \to T L(b,i)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                ranges over all morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo →
                      %mi T
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\to T 1
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi T
                      %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L : B/T1 \to A
                is the left adjoint of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi T
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo →
                      %mi T
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\to T a
                induces a unique composite
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mi b
                        %mo →
                        %mi T
                        %mi a
                        %mo →
                        %mi T
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i:b \to T a \to T 1
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(b,i)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                has a terminal object and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T:A\to B
                has a left multi-adjoint, then it is a parametric right adjoint.
          %h2#generic_morphisms Generic morphisms
          %p
            Central to the theory of parametric right adjoints is the notion of
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              \-generic
            morphisms. For any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon B\to T A
            is (strictly)
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              \-generic
            if any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+square"} commutative square
            of the following form:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi α
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mi f
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mrow
                                  %mi T
                                  %mi γ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mi T
                              %mi β
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  B
                  \&amp;
                  \\overset{\alpha}{\longrightarrow} &amp;
                  T X
                  \\\
                  \\mathllap{{}^f}
                  \\big\downarrow
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\big\downarrow
                  \\mathrlap{{}^{T\gamma}}
                  \\\
                  T A
                  \&amp;
                  \\underset{T \beta}{\longrightarrow}
                  \&amp;
                  T Z
                  }
          %p
            has a unique
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lift"} filler
            of the form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi δ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi T
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\delta \colon T A \longrightarrow T X
            = succeed "A" do
              %br/
            %strong generic factorization
            of a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon B\to T A
            is a factorization
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi g
                  %mi T
                  %mi D
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi h
                  %mi T
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  B
                  \\overset{g}{\longrightarrow}
                  T D
                  \\overset{T h}{\longrightarrow}
                  T A
          %p
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            is
            = succeed "-generic." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is a monad and any map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to T A
            has a generic factorization, then there is an induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+factorization+system"} orthogonal factorization system
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            in which
            = succeed "-generic" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is a parametric right adjoint iff every map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to T A
              has a generic factorization.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              This is Proposition 2.6 of
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Weber08"} (Weber08)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              mentioned above.
          %p P.r.a. functors between presheaf categories have an especially nice form.
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              A functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi J
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\colon [I^{op},Set] \to [J^{op},Set]
              between presheaf categories is p.r.a. iff any map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y(j)\to T 1
              has a generic factorization, where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y(j)
              is the representable presheaf on an object
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j\in J
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              This is Proposition 2.10 of
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Weber08"} (Weber08)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_T \colon y/T1 \to [I^{op},Set]
            %p
              sending an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (y(j) \to T 1)
              to the object occurring in its generic factorization. Note that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y/T1
              is equivalently the opposite of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi T
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(Z)(j) = \coprod_{x\in T1(j)} [I^{op},Set](E_T(x),Z)
            %p which preserves connected limits, since it is a coproduct of representables.
          %p
            In particular, a p.r.a. functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi I
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi J
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\colon [I^{op},Set] \to [J^{op},Set]
            is determined by giving the object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi J
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T1\in [J^{op},Set]
            together with the functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mi el
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_T\colon y/T1 = el(T1)^{op} \to [I^{op},Set]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T1(j)
            as the setof all possible “shapes” which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            allows us to “glue together” to obtain an element of shape
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_T
            as specifying exactly what each of those shapes looks like. Then the above formula for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(Z)(j)
            says that we look at all possible shapes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi T
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in T1(j)
            we can glue to get something of shape
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            we look at all the “diagrams” in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            of the corresponding shape
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_T(x)
          %p
            We can extract from this a description that is clearly a generalization of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+functor"} polynomial functor
          #AsPolynomial.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              A functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi J
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\colon [I^{op},Set] \to [J^{op},Set]
              between presheaf categories is p.r.a. iff when expressed in terms of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+fibrations"} discrete fibrations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi DFib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi d
                          %mo *
                    %mi DFib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi E
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi c
                          %mo *
                    %mi DFib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi K
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mo !
                    %mi DFib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} DFib/I \xrightarrow{d^*} DFib/E \xrightarrow{c_*} DFib/K \xrightarrow{p_!} DFib/J
            %p
              for a polynomial in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi d
                    %mi E
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi c
                    %mi K
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi p
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \xleftarrow{d} E \xrightarrow{c} K \xrightarrow{p} J
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is a discrete fibration and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d,c)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-sided+discrete+fibration"} two-sided discrete fibration
              (with in particular
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              a fibration and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              an opfibration).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T1
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo =
                      %mi el
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mn 1
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K = el(T1)^{op}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d,c)
              the two-sided Grothendieck construction of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi el
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_T\colon el(T1)^{op} \to [I^{op},Set]
              regarded as a profunctor from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi Lan
                        %mi p
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mi T
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T = Lan_p \circ Hom(E_T,-)
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Weber08"} (Weber08)
          %p
            That is, a p.r.a. functor between presheaf categories is the restriction to discrete fibrations of a certain kind of polynomial functor between slices of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            are discrete categories, then so are
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %em Cat
            are a direct generalization of p.r.a. functors between presheaf categories.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#free_categories Free categories
          %p
            Consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+category"} free category
            monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            on the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Quiv
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Quiv
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quivers"} quivers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T A
            is the quiver with the same objects as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and whose arrows are finite composable strings of arrows in
            = succeed ".." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T 1
            is the monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            regarded as a one-object category, and thus an object of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Quiv
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi T
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Quiv/T1
            is a quiver together with a natural number assigned to each edge. For any quiver
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T A \to T 1
            assigns to each composable string of arrows its length.
          %p
            The left adjoint of this functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Quiv
                  %mo →
                  %mi Quiv
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi T
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1\colon Quiv \to Quiv/T1
            takes as input a quiver with natural number “lengths” assigned to each of its arrows, and creates a new quiver by gluing together a copy of the quiver
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi …
                  %mo →
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n] = (0 \to 1 \to\dots \to n)
            (with no arrows other than those drawn) for each arrow of “length”
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is a parametric right adjoint.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Quiv
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Quiv
            is of course a presheaf category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Q
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [Q^{op},Set]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            is the category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \rightrightarrows 1
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y/T1
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ⊔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo ⊥
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N} \sqcup \{\bot\}
            and nonidentity arrows
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊥
                  %mo ⇉
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bot \rightrightarrows n
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\in\mathbb{N}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi T
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi T
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi Quiv
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_T \colon y/T1 \to Quiv
            sends
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bot
            to the quiver with one object and no arrows, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            to the quiver
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi …
                  %mo →
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n] = (0 \to 1 \to\dots \to n)
            described above.
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aurelio+Carboni"} Aurelio Carboni
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"} Peter Johnstone
              = succeed "," do
                %em Connected limits, familial representability and Artin glueing
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 5(4)
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1377312"} MR:1377312
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0960129500001183"} doi:10.1017/S0960129500001183
          %p Parametric right adjoints were introduced in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R.+Street"}> R. Street
              ,
              %em The petit topos of globular sets
              , Journal of Pure and Applied Algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 154
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-4049(99)00183-8"} doi:10.1016/S0022-4049(99)00183-8
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Weber"}> Mark Weber
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Generic morphisms, parametric representations, and weakly cartesian monads
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/13/14/13-14abs.html"} tac
            %li#Weber08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Weber"}> Mark Weber
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Familial 2-functors and parametric right adjoints
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/18/22/18-22abs.html"} tac
            %li#BMW
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clemens+Berger"}> Clemens Berger
                ,
